+export const contentTypeSnapshot: unknown = {"requirements":[{"area":"The skeleton and the row","items":[{"from":"PM","id":"T14","note":"today a type sits in three files: blocks.ts · CONFIG (3 built), content-types.ts (13, the nav, no rule reads it), messages.ts · TYPE_WORDS","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A content type is one skeleton, written once, and one row per type that adds or overrides · a new type is one row"},{"from":"PM","id":"T14b","note":"T1 (15 Oct) put the list in blocks.ts","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"The row’s home is content-types.ts · blocks.ts holds what a block is and CONFIG moves out (rule:one-responsibility) · T1 stands: one list"},{"from":"PM","id":"T14c","note":"accepts on the row · rich text reads base ∩ type ∩ field (RT5, RT8)","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A type picks the blocks it accepts and may narrow one · a block never names a type, so a new type edits no block"},{"from":"PM","id":"T9","note":"the 10 types content-types.ts names beyond the three built","ref":"15 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A type no row refines inherits the skeleton: a placeholder, created and walked through the flow like any other"}]},{"area":"People","items":[{"from":"PM","id":"RT1","note":"blocks.ts · CONFIG.people (CM, PRD, LGL) · T-E06-13","ref":"9 Oct","sheet":"","text":"Every role is held on a type, by sign-in email, in the order a dialog offers them"},{"from":"PM","id":"T85","note":"a retired rule’s, legacy/rules-retired.md (4 Nov · A)","ref":"9 Oct · RT1","sheet":"","text":"A command’s actor check reads the type of the document it names, or the type its body names when there is no document yet (T75)"},{"from":"PM","id":"T86","note":"a retired rule’s, legacy/rules-retired.md (4 Nov · A)","ref":"15 Oct · T4","sheet":"","text":"The image library is shared: its commands read a content manager of any type, an image going into a document of any type"},{"from":"PM","id":"T87","note":"the contract read groups as shared until 4 Nov (O19); the build side built T4","ref":"15 Oct · T4","sheet":"","text":"A group is its type’s: CreateGroup reads the body’s type, RenameGroup and DeleteGroup the group’s · a content manager of that type, else 403 actor.not_content_manager_of_type naming it"},{"from":"PM","id":"T13","note":"directory.ts · langs on the person · pool(FR, type) ignores the type","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A language’s reviewers are the type’s, like every role · directory.ts holds who a person is: no role, no language"},{"from":"PM","id":"T31","note":"revised 23 Oct (PM): Thomas is a content manager of every type, Baptiste in Legal on app banner too · a type’s own people, the rest as another’s: a people part once two types share a list (T23)","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"Informational’s content managers are Thomas, Jean and Guilhem, Product Jean and Guilhem · Legal and the languages’ reviewers as marketing: the same teams, its content managers excluding Dominik (T36)"},{"from":"PM","id":"T32","note":"marketing’s content managers without Dominik","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"The bottom sheet’s content managers are Jean, Guilhem and Thomas · Product, Legal and the languages’ reviewers as marketing: the same teams, its content managers excluding Dominik (T36)"}]},{"area":"The skeleton and its slots","items":[{"from":"PM","id":"T28","note":"Board, Assembly","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"The skeleton is a core every type shares and never swaps (lifecycle, roles, languages, history, export) and six slots a type fills with parts · a new need is a new part or a new slot, never the core"},{"from":"PM","id":"T29","note":"Email config, App message config, Basic components","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"Three slots are a type’s inputs: Config (1, its own fields), Components (0..1, the blocks it takes from the one library), Data (0..1, its variables) · the other three: Audience (who), Timing (when), Delivery (how)"},{"from":"PM","id":"T23","note":"a tree base → category → type lost: a diamond for each type of two families","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A type is assembled base → parts → type, read in that order for facts (ContentTypes.resolve) and sentences (Messages.of) · a type lists its parts and overrides what it must · the category stays the nav alone (T1)"},{"from":"PM","id":"T23b","note":"run every round, ported as domain tests","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"The guard: a Config or Components set is used by two types or more, an in-app type’s own by its one row (its channel has no kinds · P1, 9 Nov), a slot’s other parts by one or more · no field is set by two parts · a part reads no other part · a slot holds as many parts as it takes · lists change by add and remove (RT5)"},{"from":"PM","id":"T30","note":"closed by T79 (PM, 23 Oct · A): the bottom sheet takes the email’s components until its own render, its design comes with the build that takes it to its send · spacing is a setting of columns and stack per viewport (LY2, LY3), no block of its own","ref":"20 Oct · closed 23 Oct","sheet":"","text":"The bottom sheet takes the basic components: rich text, image, CTA, columns, stack · its layout on mobile alone (T35) · to confirm with its design"},{"from":"PM","id":"T41","note":"defined in their epic · rules then: a local name never repeats a type’s, local ones shown apart in Analytics, a local one promoted to the type in one move · not the history’s Event (glossary): a name to settle","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"Tracked events are part of the content and the document, a placeholder in E18 · a type holds its list (its channel’s built-in events and its own), a document may add local ones in Data · a CTA or a link picks its event from both, beside its action (open a link, an app screen, another sheet, close) · the results in Analytics"}]},{"area":"Languages","items":[{"from":"PM","id":"T19","note":"replaces Q13","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A type offers a language only with a reviewer for it · a check refuses the type at load: “push · IT offered, nobody reviews it”"},{"from":"PM","id":"T20","note":"the 13 Oct note “the base is not always EN” closed","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"The base stays English · a market read in one language alone (Instagram IT) is written in the default language’s slot, no translation"},{"from":"PM","id":"T21","note":"replaces Q14 · Catalog.types.langs moves into the row","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A type names the languages it offers and the ones on at creation · on ⊆ offered, each offered with a reviewer · a type offering none shows no chip"}]},{"area":"Out","items":[{"from":"PM","id":"T16","note":"content-types.ts · sendTo is an exploration · no test send anywhere","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A type names how its documents go out and its test send (an email to the person’s inbox, a push to their phone) · built in E10, named on the row now"},{"from":"PM","id":"T25","note":"sendTo leaves content-types.ts: none of it is decided","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"Where any type goes is a black box until E10 · the row keeps the slot (out.to) empty, the skeleton reads only how (Send or Publish) · informational publishes a template the system fires"},{"from":"PM","id":"T26","note":"the slot parts: send, publish · segments, trigger user · schedule, window, on action","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"What goes out is one JSON of the approved version with its full spec and each slot’s section, its shape one Export type in the contract, worked out from resolve(type)"},{"from":"PM","id":"T27","note":"open: a typed variable the tab does not hold, red or nothing","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A Data tab where a document defines the variables it uses, in rich text or typed by hand · Deblock’s own variables (a transaction’s amount) later · a placeholder to extend"},{"from":"PM","id":"T42","note":"catalog.ts · STATE holds one axis, draft review ready sent · the concept’s ready to publish, live, paused mixed the two","ref":"21 Oct","sheet":"","text":"Two states, two questions · the document state answers whether the content is ready, on each version: draft, in review, ready to publish, published · the message state answers what its delivery is doing, the delivery block’s own: sent, live, not sent, paused, finished · one word for both kinds: a version is published to its delivery"},{"from":"PM","id":"T43","note":"the delivery part is a placeholder (T16, T25) · its kinds and states are named, built in E10","ref":"21 Oct","sheet":"","text":"The delivery block plugs into the document and differs per type · its variant names the message states it reaches, a document picks it (T83): one-time not sent → scheduled → sent · automated not sent → scheduled → live ⇄ paused → finished, scheduled when it starts later · a type picks its delivery as it picks every part (T23)"},{"from":"PM","id":"T44","note":"B lost: a delivery per version, two live versions of one message to one user · A/B testing is a feature of its own, later","ref":"21 Oct · A","sheet":"","text":"One delivery per document, pointing at one version · the document carries its latest version with that version’s state, and deliveredVersion with the message state · v4 live while v5 is ready to publish: the row reads “v5 · Ready to publish” and “v4 · Live” · publishing v5 moves the pointer, the message state stays (live stays live on v5, paused stays paused)"},{"from":"PM","id":"T45","note":"answers Q42’s first question","ref":"21 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A one-time delivery is final once sent: no resume and no new version, every move refused (document.sent) · an automated delivery resumes, paused → live, and a new version publishes onto it while it is live or paused"},{"from":"PM","id":"T46","note":"B lost: Finished for both, a push sent once reading Finished","ref":"21 Oct · A","sheet":"","text":"Each kind ends in its own word · one-time: Sent, automated: Finished (stopped by hand or its window over) · both mean nothing more goes out, the rules read them alike"},{"from":"PM","id":"T47","note":"B lost: Not sent with a time, one state for nothing set and goes out on Thursday","ref":"21 Oct · A","sheet":"","text":"Scheduled is a message state of its own: published and waiting for its time, it goes out by itself · the chip reads “Scheduled · 24 Oct 9:00” · a one-time sent later, an automated one that starts later (from a date, in a window) · Publish set to Immediate skips it (T50)"},{"from":"PM","id":"T48","note":"B lost: a new time makes a new version, every approval again","ref":"21 Oct · A","sheet":"","text":"A scheduled delivery is cancelled or moved without new approvals · Cancel: scheduled → not sent, the version stays published · Reschedule: a new time, it stays scheduled · the content is approved, its time is the content manager’s (Timing is a part of its own, never the version’s)"},{"from":"PM","id":"T49","note":"B lost: a Cancelled state, two states the rules read alike","ref":"21 Oct · A","sheet":"","text":"A state says what the delivery will do, a fact says why · a cancelled schedule reads Not sent, its cancel an event in History with a line under the chip: “schedule cancelled by Thomas · 23 Oct” · Finished keeps its cause the same way (endedBy) · no Cancelled state"},{"from":"PM","id":"T50","note":"answers Q42’s automated with no start time: there is none","ref":"21 Oct","sheet":"","text":"Publish needs its delivery’s time, set in Delivery: Immediate or Scheduled (a date and time) · no Publish without one · a confirm before Publish says what will happen: one-time “Goes out now” or “Goes out on 24 Oct, 9:00”, automated “Goes live now” or “Goes live on 1 Aug, 9:00” · its lines land in messages.ts with E18’s ticket"},{"from":"PM","id":"T51","note":"B lost: a shared template automations point at, one Publish moving every live delivery · reads against four eyes (4E1, 4E2: one approval in person, not by the author): from a template, two at least","ref":"21 Oct · A","sheet":"","text":"A template is a starting point: a document with no delivery, it is never sent · Create from template copies its content into a new document, which sets its own delivery (trigger, audience, timing) and then lives on its own · a document made from a template gathers at least two approvals before Publish · templates a placeholder in E18"},{"from":"PM","id":"T52","note":"the active period is Timing’s (T54) · Audience holds the segment","ref":"21 Oct","sheet":"","text":"What starts an automated delivery is its trigger, a placeholder in Delivery · a system event (card activated, a transfer received, with a delay or not) · a person’s action in the app (a screen opened, a first transfer) · entering a segment (inactive for 30 days) · a date in the person’s data (birthday, a card expiring) · a cycle (every Monday, 9:00) · a market event (BTC past a price) · limits on any: a frequency cap, quiet hours · a sequence of documents (a journey) is no delivery, an epic of its own"},{"from":"PM","id":"T53","note":"B lost: Finished for good and Duplicate to run again, an approved banner approved again because 31 Aug passed · replaces T49’s endedBy: a window ends it, a person pauses it · both states kept (PM, 21 Oct · B): Paused is a decision pending, Finished is done, the list shows which without the line under the chip","ref":"21 Oct · A","sheet":"","text":"Finished means its time is over: its active period past its end · an automated delivery with no end never finishes, it is live or paused · stopping by hand is Paused · Reschedule with a new time brings it back, finished → scheduled or live, with no approvals (T48) · Analytics splits its numbers by period"},{"from":"PM","id":"T54","note":"the five setups: automated always (an event, at once, no end) · automated from a date · automated in a window (an end: Finished) · one-time now · one-time at a time","ref":"21 Oct · A","sheet":"","text":"An automated delivery is two settings: its trigger, what sends each message (T52, a cycle among them), and its active period, when it is on: a start (at once or a date) and an end (none or a date) · Finished comes from the end alone, no end never finishes · a one-time delivery has no trigger, one moment: now or at a time · time is no trigger"},{"from":"PM","id":"T55","note":"B lost: a folder per module, its facts, rules, words and colours together, the layers broken and the words in N files · first step: delivery-flow.ts","ref":"21 Oct · A","sheet":"","text":"A document is a base every document has (who it is, its versions and their state, its approvals, its languages, its history) and the modules its type attaches: Config, Components, Data, Events, Audience, Timing, Delivery, People · a template attaches no Delivery, Timing or Audience · data driven, never folder driven: content-modules.ts lists the modules, a module with behaviour has one rules file (Delivery: delivery-flow.ts, Components: blocks.ts and block-rules.ts), its words and colours in messages.ts and gate-states.ts under its key"},{"from":"PM","id":"T56","note":"B lost: Approvals and Translations alone, versions and history kept in the base","ref":"21 Oct · A","sheet":"","text":"The base is who a document is: its id, its type, its group, its name · everything else is a module its type attaches · the core’s rows became modules: Approvals, Translations, Versions and History, the last two always attached · export goes out with Delivery, the tabs come from the modules, the placeholders stay the skeleton’s rule (T9)"},{"from":"PM","id":"T57","note":"B lost: a language’s approval in Translations, the approval mechanism in two modules · a type with no Translations has no language gate (Instagram IT, T20)","ref":"21 Oct · A","sheet":"","text":"Three modules, three questions · People: who, a team per role, a language’s reviewers among them · Approvals: what is approved before it goes out, Product, Legal and a gate per language carried, one mechanism for every gate (gate-rules.ts) · Translations: which languages and their text (translation-flow.ts) · a language’s approval is Approvals’, its text Translations’ · a module reads another in a fixed order, People → Translations → Approvals, never a loop"},{"from":"PM","id":"T58","note":"B lost: Timing a module of its own, its kind checked against Delivery’s, one fact twice","ref":"21 Oct · A","sheet":"","text":"Timing and trigger are Delivery’s: a delivery variant names its kind, the times a document picks (one-time: now, at a time · automated: always, from a date, in a window) and, on its row, the triggers it takes · the board has three zones: Content, in the version and approved with it (Config, Components, Data, Events, Translations) · Delivery, outside the version, changed with no approval (Audience, Delivery, T48) · Process, who works on it and how it is approved (People, Approvals, Versions, History) · a module’s zone is its group, data driven"},{"from":"PM","id":"T59","note":"B lost: the standing alone, the types to define unseen","ref":"21 Oct · A","sheet":"","text":"The board shows each module’s standing, worked out from the data: no rule file, a placeholder · a rule whose person moves name commands commands.ts lacks, rule only · otherwise mechanics · a type with no config of its own reads to define on its variants · a command added to the contract turns the module by itself"},{"from":"PM","id":"T60","note":"closes Q42 · a Replaced state lost: the message chip already names the live version","ref":"21 Oct","sheet":"","text":"No version is marked replaced · the row reads two chips, each with its version: the message, Live v5 · the document, its latest version’s state, In review v6 · Publish moves the delivery to any newer approved version, v5 to v8, the ones between never sent · a version’s own past is History’s (published 12 Oct, replaced by v8 on 21 Oct), never a state"},{"from":"PM","id":"T61","note":"B lost: optional, a warning in the confirm, a Live delivery that sends nothing","ref":"21 Oct · A","sheet":"","text":"An automated delivery needs its trigger before Publish, as it needs its time (T50) · Publish greys with its refusal, delivery.no_trigger, “Pick what sends it in Delivery” · the confirm names it: “Goes live now · sends each time a card is activated” · a type names the kinds of trigger it takes, a document picks its own (E10)"},{"from":"PM","id":"T62","note":"B lost: an Export module of its own, never without a delivery","ref":"21 Oct · A","sheet":"","text":"Export is the document’s and Delivery sends it (PM, 28 Oct · was Delivery’s): sending hands one package to a middleware bucket, the approved version as one JSON with its full spec and each module’s section (T26) · both kinds hand it over, send once, publish for the system to fire · the bucket a black box until E10 (T25) · a type with no delivery has no export"},{"from":"PM","id":"T63","note":"A lost: a Delivery move to the person alone, no group and no test without a delivery · replaces T16’s test send on Delivery","ref":"21 Oct · B","sheet":"","text":"Testing is a module of its own: while it is being written, a document is sent to a test group of user ids · any version, a draft too, no approval, the delivery’s state unmoved · each test a line in History (“test sent to the test group · v2”) · the group’s shape in E10 · a template can be tested, it attaches no Delivery"},{"from":"PM","id":"T65","note":"B lost: a button on the bar, the test group with nowhere to be set","ref":"21 Oct · A","sheet":"","text":"Testing brings a tab of its own, as every module with settings does: the test group to set, the send, the tests sent so far · a placeholder until E10 · no test button on the bar"},{"from":"PM","id":"T66","note":"B lost: Schedule, a tab whose name covers the time alone","ref":"21 Oct · A","sheet":"","text":"A tab is named as the module that brings it: Delivery’s tab is Delivery, with its time, its trigger and its export (T58, T62) · replaces Schedule in T38"},{"from":"PM","id":"T67","note":"a core tab with no module lost: the one tab no module answered for","ref":"21 Oct","sheet":"","text":"Analytics is a module, always attached: its Results variant brings the Analytics tab, how the message did once it went out, each tracked event it defines among them (T41) · History’s variant brings the History tab · no tab is core but Content, which the content modules fill · the tab words live in messages.ts · SCREEN.tabs"},{"from":"PM","id":"T68","note":"extends T27, which gave Data to informational alone","ref":"21 Oct","sheet":"","text":"Every message type attaches Data, marketing as informational: a marketing document defines its variables too (a first name, an amount) · the tab is there on every type, greyed while the document uses none (its shape in E18) · templates attach none"},{"from":"PM","id":"T69","note":"A lost: a type per kind, 12 rows, every content change in three places and a template that can drift from its marketing · revises T22, T64","ref":"21 Oct · B","sheet":"","text":"A type is a channel (Email, App banners, Bottom sheets, Push) · its kind is the document’s, fixed at creation: marketing, informational or template, by who may get it (T83) · the type’s row holds its content modules once and the kinds it offers, each kind its own config: its delivery (segments and send or publish, a trigger and publish, none for a template) and its narrowing (people, gates) · the nav lists a type by kind · a template is a copy, no link: Use template makes a marketing document or informational of the same type"},{"from":"PM","id":"T70","note":"replaces T12 (PM, confirmed 23 Oct: the type page’s Add) · an empty groupId lost: two ways to say no group","ref":"21 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A group is required: every list (a type, its kind) holds one default group, No group, that every document without another sits in · No group is always last, never renamed, never deleted, drawn only when it holds a document · New document picks its group: the groups of its list and No group, the group the reader started from preselected (its + on a group card), No group from the page’s own button · the type stays fixed (T75) · a document’s group never empty (T5): the API may leave it out, the document lands in No group (T75)"},{"from":"PM","id":"T72","note":"replaces T38’s Analytics on every type","ref":"21 Oct","sheet":"","text":"Analytics comes with a delivery: the results of what went out · a template is never sent (T51), so it attaches no Audience, Delivery or Analytics, and its tabs are Content, Testing and History · on the board a socket with nothing plugged in greys, a template’s delivery sockets read “never sent”"},{"from":"PM","id":"T73","note":"revises T72’s template tabs","ref":"21 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A template attaches Data: its content may use variables, a copy inherits them · its tabs are Content, Data, Testing and History · Audience, Delivery and Analytics greyed (T72) · Data a placeholder until E10"},{"from":"PM","id":"T74","note":"replaces T-E06-13 c13 (roleLabel summed every type) and T-E01-03 c2’s roleLabel on the wire","ref":"22 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A role is a type’s, never a person’s · directory.ts holds who a person is: name, face, emails, no role and no language · inside a document a role reads the document’s type (“Reviewer · FR” on Email · Marketing) · outside one, the profile menu, the people list, GET /directory, a person shows name and email, no role"},{"from":"PM","id":"T75","note":"replaces T3 (the body named no type, PM 15 Oct)","ref":"23 Oct","sheet":"","text":"CreateDocument names its type and its kind, both required · the group is optional: left out, the document lands in No group of its list (T70) · named, it must be of the same type and kind, else 409 group.other_type or group.other_kind · a document says what it is, through the screen or the API, and a wrong group is refused, never followed"},{"from":"PM","id":"T76","note":"T34: the contract describes a type’s shape, never the list · an agent reads the types off its MCP tools’ description (PM, 23 Oct)","ref":"23 Oct","sheet":"","text":"No query lists the types · the list is content-types.ts’, in the build: every type brings its own logic and is built one at a time, so a new type is a row and a build, never an answer the server gives"},{"from":"PM","id":"T77","note":"T51: Create from template","ref":"23 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A copy keeps its source’s kind; only a template starts another: a template copies into a marketing document, an informational or a template, a marketing document or an informational into its own kind · else 409 document.other_kind · the kinds a copy may become are a list on each kind (content-types.ts · KINDS · copiesInto), so any kind into any later is that list, never the contract"},{"from":"PM","id":"T78","note":"T69: a type is a channel · the channel ids banners, sheets became appBanner, bottomSheet, each its marketing row’s key","ref":"23 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A document’s type is its channel (email, appBanner, bottomSheet, push, a placeholder’s own key), its kind apart (marketing, informational, template) · the API names both, a row of content-types.ts is the pair (rowOf) · a new family or a new kind is a row, never a new field: Social, Pages and Legal take kinds when they are designed"},{"from":"PM","id":"T79","note":"revises T39: the skeleton fills the kinds made of parts already built","ref":"23 Oct","sheet":"","text":"E18 builds every kind of the four message channels: email, appBanner, bottomSheet and push, each marketing, informational and template · what they share is built once: the content (config, components), the library, the group, the editor · their delivery stays a placeholder until E10 · a bottom sheet takes the email’s components and its preview until its own mobile render"},{"from":"PM","id":"T80","note":"replaces T8’s /email/marketing and T9a’s /app/app-banner: the type is the channel, its kind apart (T64, T78)","ref":"23 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A document’s address is /{channel}/{kind}/{group}/{document}: /email/marketing, /push/informational, /bottom-sheet/templates, then a group, then a document · the channel’s id in kebab case, the kind’s path (content-types.ts · KINDS) · a group and a document each its name then its own id, summer-insurance-m2p8q1zd, mailing-standard-k3f9x2ab (T2, T8), so each has a link to send · the router reads the last id alone, a group’s link holding after a Rename, a document’s after a Move, a document unique across every document (FD5b) and standing on its own: what comes before is drawn from the data and replaced in place after a Move or a Rename (T8) · type 2 segments, group 3, document 4"},{"from":"PM","id":"T81","note":"T70: No group always last, never renamed, never deleted","ref":"27 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A document moves into No group as into any group of its list: No group is the list’s default group (T70) · the Move dialog offers it last, as the type page draws it"},{"from":"PM","id":"T83","note":"revises T43, T64, T69: campaign and transactional, a kind that was how it went out","ref":"27 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A document’s kind says who may get it: marketing, sent only to those who agreed to its topic, or informational, sent to everyone; a template is never sent · the rule: can a person opt out of it? yes, marketing; no, informational · how it goes out is Delivery’s, the same for both: every delivering row offers both audiences and both deliveries, its first the default, a document picks one · urgency is a priority, never a kind"},{"from":"PM","id":"T82","note":"T70: one per list, last, never renamed, never deleted","ref":"27 Oct","sheet":"","text":"No group is written with its list: the migration and the seed write one per built row of content-types.ts, and a row added later brings its own in the same migration · never written by a command, never by a read · every built row holds exactly one"},{"from":"PM","id":"T84","note":"E18 report, question 3","ref":"3 Nov · R2 Q3 · A","sheet":"","text":"New document’s GROUP finds a group as Move to… does: groups by name, paged, Search groups and the no-match line · one searchable field of the form that opens its matches · the look is the spec’s"},{"from":"PM","id":"T64","note":"revises T9a’s key: email becomes campaigns, not marketing","ref":"21 Oct","sheet":"","text":"Email’s first kind is Marketing, key marketing: /email/marketing, beside Informational · one word with the concept and the meeting (21 Oct)"}]},{"area":"Files and words","items":[{"from":"PM","id":"T17","note":"the test: a translation changes messages alone, a process change facts or rules alone","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"Business and presentation apart: facts, rules and the glossary are the business, sentences, colours and views are how the app says it · a type’s sentences are a dictionary beside the base, Messages.of(type) reading the type’s line first"},{"from":"PM","id":"T24","note":"a file per type lost: ~70 helmets, or an async loader · the Files board is the per-type view","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"One file per kind of fact, the types as its entries: content-types.ts (skeleton, rows), content-modules.ts (new, the modules and their variants · T55), blocks.ts (blocks alone), directory.ts (persons alone), messages.ts (base), messages-content.ts (new, the parts’ and the types’ lines)"},{"from":"PM","id":"T18","note":"today one loop of six files, plan-Data map draws it","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"Seven layers, a file reads only the ones below: words · look · contract · facts · rules · examples and tests · views · a read upwards or a loop is the guard’s finding (rule:layers-read-downward)"},{"from":"PM","id":"T18b","note":"gate-rules.ts · gatesOf, screen-view.ts × 3: the guard’s ratchet starts at 4","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"No rule and no view branches on a type’s name · it reads the type’s row"}]},{"area":"The page","items":[{"from":"PM","id":"T15","note":"this page · Board, Files, Assembly","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"Content type logic draws the skeleton, each type’s assembly, its files and the checks, all read from the data"}]},{"area":"Scope","items":[{"from":"PM","id":"T22","note":"two to define: informational, bottom sheet","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"The first types are Email (marketing, informational) and App messages (banner, bottom sheet, push) · Social, Pages and Legal stay placeholders · nothing in the skeleton may assume a type is a message"}]},{"area":"Open","items":[{"from":"PM","id":"T33","note":"replaces Q27 · field-kinds.ts, its line in messages.ts, its refusal · built with the Data tab (T27)","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A variable typed in a field that the Data tab does not hold marks the field red: “{amout} is not in Data” · a field check like a link that does not resolve, Create version greyed until it is fixed (VL1) · one validator for text and rich text"},{"from":"PM","id":"T34","note":"replaces Q17 · for CC: content-types.ts a fixture the server reads at start, later the content_types table and its seed · a test: every document’s type is known","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A document’s type is a key checked against content-types.ts, not a closed union in the contract · ContentType = string, an unknown key refused as type.unknown · the contract describes a row’s shape (TypeSpec), never the list · a new type is a row, the contract and the build untouched"},{"from":"PM","id":"T35","note":"replaces Q30 · LY1’s “on mobile a Columns stacks” and LY3’s “an empty one renders stacked” go: no automatic layout · a new block starts with a default per viewport · CC: the rename and a migration of stored block types, in E18 after E09’s report","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A block defines what it is and how it shows in each viewport: desktop and mobile, tablet later, each its own explicit props, nothing worked out automatically · a type narrows a block’s viewports as it narrows rich text (RT5: block ∩ type): the bottom sheet’s columns on mobile alone · the panel and the preview show the viewports left · emailColumns and emailStack became columns and stack (23 Oct), a block names no type (T14c) · LY1 refined: a layout block is shared while its fields fit, a new one only when they differ"},{"from":"PM","id":"T36","note":"replaces Q31 · Content managers, Product team, Legal team, Translators, each used by 5 types · informational excludes Thomas and Dominik from the content managers, the banner Thomas and Dominik, and Baptiste from Legal, the bottom sheet Dominik · peopleAsIn gone: no type reads another’s row","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"People are teams: a team is people with one role, in the order a dialog offers them (RT1) · a type picks one team per role and may exclude members by sign-in email (team ∩ type, as RT5 and T35 narrow) · a new member of a team joins every type that picks it, unless excluded · the guard: every role held by one team, an exclude names a member, nobody left is a finding (T19)"},{"from":"PM","id":"T37","note":"replaces Q20 · a Legal team per language is not something Deblock will have","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"A document written in another language in the default slot (Instagram IT) is approved by Product and Legal as always · no team per language for the gates"},{"from":"PM","id":"T38","note":"the backlog’s 14 Oct story read Template, Audiences, Schedule, Analytics, Logs · rewritten · bodies: Audience and Schedule E10, Analytics later, History E11","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"The editor’s tabs are its modules’, in content-modules.ts · TABS’ order: a tab is named as the module that brings it (T66) · Content on every type, every other tab brought by a module the type attaches (T28) · Diff on Content"},{"from":"PM","id":"T39","note":"Segments, Trigger user, Schedule, Window, On action, Send, Publish and Data filled in their epics (E10, E11, later) · T33’s check built with the Data tab","ref":"20 Oct","sheet":"","text":"E18 builds the skeleton and fills none of it · what is built stays as it is: Content (today’s editor), 